    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-16208" textLabel="epoxide hydrolase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LZ31" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">An epoxide hydrolase activity was detected in microsomes isolated from Arabidopsis seedlings. The activity was also found in the cytosol fraction. The epoxide hydrolase was able to convert epoxides generated by CYP77A4 to their corresponding diols |CITS: [19120447]|. The catalytic activity of CYP77A4 was demonstrated by incubating radiolabeled free fatty acids with microsomes from yeast expressing CYP77A4. CYP77A4 catalyzed epoxidation of oleate, linoleate and linolenate, but not saturated stearate. In addition, CYP77A4 also had fatty acid in-chain hydroxylase activity towards laureate and oleate. The enzyme activities were NADPH-dependent |CITS: [19120447]|. It is noteworthy that CYP77A4 differs from CYP726A1, an enzyme identified in E. lagaseae. CYP726A1 was able to epoxidize linoleate incorporated into phosphatidylcholine, whereas CYP77A4 metabolizes free fatty acids.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-16208" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G04660.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9LZ31" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP77A4" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33910, RXN-18706, RXN-18705, RXN-18704, RXN-18703, RXN-18702, RXN-18701, RXN-18710, RXN-18709, RXN-18708, RXN-18707" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="11" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005792" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G04660.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G04660" />
